  // ==========================================================================
  // Container-file delivery (VHD / VHDX / ISO / IMG)
  //
  // Generic container tradecraft, backing the DEAD#VAX rules above. Mounting a
  // container IS the Mark-of-the-Web bypass: the .vhd itself gets a
  // Zone.Identifier on download, but Windows mounts it as a separate volume and
  // the files inside inherit nothing — to the OS they are ordinary local files
  // on a local disk, so SmartScreen never prompts.
  // ==========================================================================

  {
    "name": "Disk image mounted",
    "description": "VHD/VHDX/ISO mounted — container delivery bypasses Mark-of-the-Web entirely, so nothing inside the image carries a Zone.Identifier or triggers SmartScreen",
